<figure class="text-figure" data-candidates aria-labelledby="candidates-title">
  <figcaption id="candidates-title"><span class="figure-number">Figure 3</span> The same index keys, different matches</figcaption>
  <label class="figure-option">Request <select data-request aria-label="Request"><option value="and">blue and mugs · anywhere</option><option value="phrase">blue mugs · phrase</option></select></label>
  <p class="representation" data-query data-live>'blue' &amp; 'mug'</p>
  <div class="posting-lists">
    <p><strong>blue</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> → </span><span data-posting="0">A · B · C</span></p>
    <p><strong>mug</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> → </span><span data-posting="1">A · B · C</span></p>
  </div>
  <p class="scene-label">Heap documents · positions retained in their vectors</p>
  <div class="diagnostic-rows" data-live>
    <div data-row="0"><strong>A</strong><span>The <b>blue₂ mugs₃</b></span><span data-status="0">not visited</span></div>
    <div data-row="1"><strong>B</strong><span><b>Blue₁</b> ceramic₂ <b>mugs₃</b></span><span data-status="1">not visited</span></div>
    <div data-row="2"><strong>C</strong><span><b>Mugs₁</b> in₂ <b>blue₃</b></span><span data-status="2">not visited</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="query-check" data-count data-live>0 candidates collected</p>
  <p class="step-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">All three documents have both lexemes. GIN keeps a posting list of row locations for each key.</p>
  <div class="player" role="group" aria-label="Figure 3 playback"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div><div class="hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  <p class="figure-note">Three separate diagnostic snippets, not extra shop products. A/B/C stand for row locations. This drawing models matching information, not physical GIN pages or an execution schedule.</p>
  <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><p>Both keys point to A, B and C. Intersecting their posting lists retains all three. For blue AND mug, every document matches. For the phrase blue followed immediately by mug, the vectors prove only A: blue at 2, mug at 3. B has a gap and C has the reverse order. The index keys alone cannot make that distinction.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-candidates]')){
  const request=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-request]')!;
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw(step:number){
    const phrase=request.value==='phrase';
    root.querySelector('[data-query]')!.textContent=phrase?"'blue' <-> 'mug'":"'blue' & 'mug'";
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-posting]').forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('selected',step>i));
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-status]').forEach((el,i)=>{el.textContent=step<2?'not visited':step===2?'candidate':(!phrase||i===0)?'match':'recheck rejects';root.querySelector(`[data-row="${i}"]`)!.classList.toggle('rejected',step===3&&phrase&&i!==0)});
    root.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=step<2?'0 candidates collected':step===2?'3 candidates · positions not yet checked':phrase?'3 candidates → 1 phrase match':'3 candidates → 3 membership matches';
    root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=[
      'All three documents have both lexemes. GIN keeps a posting list of row locations for each key.',
      'Read the blue list, then the mug list. The same three row locations occur in both.',
      'The intersection retains A, B and C. These keys carry no word positions or field weights.',
      phrase?'Read the vectors to check order and distance. Only A has mug immediately after blue. B and C are rejected.':'For ordinary membership, both exact keys establish the text predicate. Heap access still supplies visible rows and returned values.'
    ][step];
  }});request.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
}
</script>
